######## probe::chain_accuracy_needs_an_intermediate_wider_than_the_operand_type
  control = "None was run as a case that had to fail. The two instruments are at different widths 
  and fraction widths by different authors, so what stands in place of a control is that the 
  growth rate agrees across a change of both, which a single-width sweep could not have shown. 
  What neither arm carries is a chain shape on which the width must NOT grow, and without one the 
  linear growth is measured rather than isolated."
